id: pm-xtq2
title: Align pm-presets with pm 2026.8.7 and harden merge-driver lifecycle
description: "Adopt the current pm CLI/SDK and pm-changelog, install the canonical generated-extension merge fence, replace the authored JavaScript lifecycle helper with erasable TypeScript, and prove POSIX and real Windows command resolution without conflating this bounded compatibility tranche with full release readiness."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 0
tags[6]: merge-safety,multi-agent,pm-cli-2026.8.7,release-gate,typescript,windows
created_at: "2026-08-07T19:45:48.641Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-07T20:09:18.045Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-07T20:06:26.386Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-07T20:06:26.386Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: The lockfile resolves @unbrained/pm-cli and pm-changelog 2026.8.7 and the peer floor is 2026.8.7; pm merge install emits extensions/** -merge and scopes pm-json to .managed-extensions.json; lifecycle source is erasable TypeScript with no dynamic imports and resolves target-platform PATH/PATHEXT safely; npm ci runs the real prepare hook on windows-latest with a real cmd shim under a spaced and percent-delimited path; lifecycle tests reach exact 100/100/100; npm and Bun package gates plus fresh packed-artifact installed-pm acceptance pass; privacy/history and full-source quality limits are tracked independently; exact-head bot review is dispositioned before merge
definition_of_ready: "Canonical main is clean and unique, no open package item or PR duplicates this tranche, installed and registry pm are 2026.8.7, and the baseline release gate is measured honestly."
value: Concurrent agents get deterministic PM extension-asset merge semantics from installs on supported platforms.
impact: Prevents generated extension assets from entering semantic field merges and makes lifecycle failures observable on Windows.
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "Aligned pm CLI/SDK and pm-changelog to 2026.8.7, installed the canonical extension fence, replaced the JavaScript prepare guard with exact-covered erasable TypeScript, added immutable-action Windows CI, and completed npm/Bun/fresh-artifact acceptance plus exact-head review disposition."
expected_result: "pm-presets installs canonical pm 2026.8.7 merge semantics and runs a portable fail-loud prepare lifecycle whose Windows dispatch is proven through the real command parser, without overstating broader release readiness."
actual_result: "The package now resolves pm CLI/SDK and pm-changelog 2026.8.7, protects generated extension assets with the canonical fence, runs an erasable TypeScript lifecycle with target-platform PATH/PATHEXT semantics, and adds a real windows-latest cmd.exe integration gate. npm and Bun release checks each pass 59 tests with zero skips; the lifecycle source is exact 100/100/100; a fresh packed artifact installs into pm 2026.8.7, exposes all seven presets, applies agent-workflow, creates a real AgentRun item, and validates. Independent pm-915f and pm-vsn5 preserve the all-source quality and history-privacy blockers, so no publication is authorized."
